nts admitted to hospital for covid  were prescribed an antimicrobial but  only seven percent needed them certainly  there have been a couple of studies that  have shown that antibiotic-resistant  organisms in hospital settings have been  on the rise through this pandemic  as for jeff after years of having cf and  a superbug his lungs were ravaged he  needed a double lung transplant to live  jeff says the doctors told him the  superbug would make his surgery more  dangerous  we knew going in that the the big battle  would be the bacterial battle there's  only a 50 chance of survivability one  year post-transplant  despite the odds he had the life-saving  transplant in 2018. jeff knows if his  antibiotic-resistant superbug causes a  flare-up again it's likely there are no  more drug treatment options to keep him  alive what's the feeling that you carry  with you along with the odds every day  of your life  right now it's gratefulness  i'm still here  candace daniel global news  next on global national with valentine's  day approaching new research shows which  gender is hit harder by heartbreak  [Music]  as many canadians prepare to celebrate  valentine's day with their partners  others might be newly single fresh off a  breakup and alone  a new study out of the university of  british columbia found when men leave a  relationship they seem to be at greater  risk of mental illness and as jamie  morocco explains the pandemic could be  making things worse  when toronto relationship coach roman  mironov's marriage ended seven years ago  he says he was devastated he fell into a  mild depression i felt like that was the  end of my life for for the first couple  of weeks i felt terrible and i just  didn't know what to do researchers from  the university of british columbia have  found when relationships break down men  are at an increased risk of anxiety  depression and even suicide compared to  women of 47 canadian and australian  participants 96 share those feelings and  accounts john oliver professor of  nursing and lead author on the study  says the risk of male suicide quadruples  after a marital separation  if we think about suicide prevention  and knowing that men's suicide at three  to four times the rate of women i think  it's such  a given that the relationship breakdowns  do put men at risk the covenant 19  pandemic is only making the situation  worse for many men the study found they  are turning to substance use drinking to  cope and because of social restrictions  they are losing close ties with friends  ottawa psychotherapist sean hale offers  sessions online and says he's seeing the  same thing in his practice after a  breakup  if you're feeling these emotions and you  can't get them out  they can lead into those kind of  feelings of depression because you're  kind of dealing with it on your own olaf  says there needs to be more mental  health care options geared to men he  hopes to see people reach out before a  breakup gaining valuable communication  and coping skills strategies for working  through those things and and splitting  amicably  and then working their way through  through those uh those challenging  situations mironov agrees the 39 year  old now has a new partner and uses his  experience to help others don't go into  that vicious cycle break out of it by  reaching out to someone a decision  experts say could be life-saving jamie  morocco global news toronto  coming up dream job how a canadian  former hockey player and his partner  became the caretakers of a remote irish  island  believing in yourself might just get you  to the olympic podium and that is  certainly the case for canada steven  dubois who added a bronze to his metal  count in 500 meters short track  following his skate dubois said he knew  he had the potential to win medals he  almost didn't qualify for the final  though after a collision with a south  korean skater but after review south  korea was penalized for an illegal late  pass and the rest is history  as we hopefully begin to emerge from the  pandemic many of us are eager to put  isolation behind us and resume our  normal lives but a former pro hockey  player from saskatchewan and his dutch  girlfriend are doing pretty much the  opposite they beat out thousands of  other applicants to become caretakers of  an uninhabited island off the coast of  ireland redmond shannon has their story  it's a shot at tips today  [Applause]  in a decade of minor league hockey brock  montgomery scored plenty of goals and  through his fair share of punches too  and there's going to be a fight  montgomery off the ice he practiced yoga  and mindfulness to deal with the stress  playing professionally in the  netherlands he met claire de haas  traveling together just before the  pandemic claire saw a job ad caretakers  wanted for summer cottages on a small  irish island i showed brock immediately  and then he said  where can we apply and we apply the next  day the only problem thousands of others  did too and then covered 19 hit  stranding them on an indonesian island  it was kind of surreal because we had  the island  to ourselves for a little bit there  something that will never happen again  they stayed there for months and  volunteered before heading to canada and  back to europe this year a few weeks ago  we got a message from them  if we were still in and we immediately  said yes now as restrictions ease for  the rest of us brock and claire are  going into self-imposed exile off the  grid for six months so there will be a  solar panel that gives us enough to  charge our phones our laptop and stuff  like that  and they bring food to us every day  although solar panels may only go so far  in an irish summer claire's always  joking that we're not made of sugar  she's dodged so yeah so we're expecting  we're expecting some rain seclusion has  perhaps one major challenge for any  couple it's like we're not we're not  leaving so yeah just have to get used to  it and enjoy not kill each other  that mindfulness training may come in  very handy and if brock ever feels  homesick he can just squint into the  atlantic sunset over the next island  over known here as the sleeping giant  next stop canada redmond shannon double  news london  and that is global national for this  sunday night i'm chris galas tonight  your canada is peggy's cove nova scotia  thanks for watching everyone donna  friesen is back tomorrow hope you have a  great night  [Applause]  [Music]
 

